    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the tenure requirement for membership level 4 in `MembershipLevels.of(Owner)` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/common/MembershipLevels.java`).\n\n**The change:**\n- The level accumulates one point for each pre-tenure factor: an email, a `namesakeCount` of 0, and a household of three or more members (`householdSize >= 3`). These factors alone are capped at level 3 (`MAX_PRE_TENURE_LEVEL`).\n- Level 4 (`TOP_LEVEL`) is now gated behind tenure: it requires strictly more than 365 days (`TENURE_DAYS_FOR_TOP_LEVEL`) between the owner's `registrationDate` and today.\n\n**Why the household factor:** the specification's illustration \u2014 \"a new owner with an email, a namesakeCount of 0 and a 3-member household is level 3, not 4\" \u2014 only makes sense if the household is a factor that *would* push the level to 4. Email + namesake alone already max at 3, so without household contributing there would be no would-be-4 to cap. Adding it makes the tenure gate meaningful: a fully-qualified new owner computes to 4 on factors but is capped at 3 because a newly created owner's registration date is today (zero tenure).\n\nThe new `coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` acceptance test and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`). `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the repository.",
